WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:06.590 --> 00:00:08.550
- So, what do we do now?

00:00:08.634 --> 00:00:10.135
Do we need to report it?

00:00:10.219 --> 00:00:12.596
He's been accused
and we know about it.

00:00:12.679 --> 00:00:14.348
- It's not a credible accusation.

00:00:19.645 --> 00:00:22.523
- Although it worked perfectly
as a novel,

00:00:22.606 --> 00:00:25.150
when you adapt it into a series,
it changes.

00:00:26.109 --> 00:00:29.196
We created a show that has
a very strong aesthetic.

00:00:30.614 --> 00:00:32.574
We exposed for the outside world,

00:00:32.658 --> 00:00:34.952
and made the people silhouettey and dark.

00:00:36.078 --> 00:00:37.454
Stuck in their own prison.

00:00:38.789 --> 00:00:41.500
- Since we have Morten directing
all eight episodes,

00:00:41.583 --> 00:00:44.711
it really has a uniformity
of directorial vision.

00:00:44.795 --> 00:00:46.839
And it feels
incredibly cinematic.

00:00:48.090 --> 00:00:50.634
Same for our costume designer,
whose challenge is

00:00:50.717 --> 00:00:53.512
how do I make them feel
as realistic as possible?

00:00:54.263 --> 00:00:56.181
- They're saying
he looks smug and remorseless.

00:00:56.265 --> 00:00:58.350
He's not even 15 years old.

00:00:58.433 --> 00:01:02.271
- It's a murder mystery
that is all about the characters,

00:01:02.354 --> 00:01:03.564
how they experience it.

00:01:03.647 --> 00:01:07.067
- One of our challenges was how
do I not create a parody of these people?

00:01:07.150 --> 00:01:09.069
How do I really do justice to them?

00:01:09.152 --> 00:01:12.656
- How could this even happen?
I can't get my head around it.

00:01:13.740 --> 00:01:15.367
- I don't know how many times
we've been sitting behind the monitor,

00:01:15.450 --> 00:01:17.786
and we thought,
"We actually got the perfect Andy."

00:01:18.662 --> 00:01:22.791
Chris brings both a strength
and a vulnerability to the character,

00:01:22.875 --> 00:01:24.668
which is really hard.

00:01:24.751 --> 00:01:25.919
- I knew my son.

00:01:26.003 --> 00:01:27.713
- That's it?
That's your justification?

00:01:27.796 --> 00:01:29.298
- I was being a father.

00:01:29.381 --> 00:01:32.801
- And Michelle is just so open
and very honest.

00:01:33.760 --> 00:01:35.888
And between Jaeden
and the other actors, everyone,

00:01:35.971 --> 00:01:37.848
they're so fantastic.

00:01:37.931 --> 00:01:41.518
- Remember that in their eyes,
it isn't just Jacob who's guilty.

00:01:41.602 --> 00:01:43.020
You all are.

00:01:43.812 --> 00:01:46.273
- These actors have that ability,

00:01:46.356 --> 00:01:49.735
not just to embody
the complexity of these characters,

00:01:49.818 --> 00:01:53.238
but to project out from the screen
and to connect with the viewer.

00:01:56.158 --> 00:01:57.743
- It's sort of like
doing a play.

00:01:57.826 --> 00:02:01.246
It's, you know, you have these kind of
big, long, two-hander scenes

00:02:01.330 --> 00:02:02.998
which are written so brilliantly.

00:02:04.082 --> 00:02:08.086
- If you think about the complexity
of scripting eight hours,

00:02:08.170 --> 00:02:09.713
you're building a Swiss watch.

00:02:09.796 --> 00:02:11.089
- Start from the beginning.

00:02:12.591 --> 00:02:16.261
- It was a really cohesive team,
and it all came from this place

00:02:16.345 --> 00:02:19.097
that we're just in love
with this story and these characters.

00:02:20.432 --> 00:02:23.143
- And that's very exciting to me,
to see this world

00:02:23.227 --> 00:02:27.022
really developed in a vivid
and full and complete way.

00:02:27.898 --> 00:02:30.776
- It's a character-driven,
intense thriller.

00:02:30.859 --> 00:02:34.738
All these twists and turns, you just
hold on to it and go on this ride.

00:02:35.781 --> 00:02:38.450
- You're ruining his life.
You're gonna destroy it.

00:02:38.534 --> 00:02:40.869
- There is more going on here
than you're aware of.

00:02:40.953 --> 00:02:42.788
- More than what?
Tell me, goddamn it!

